    EXCEPTION — this plan was authored retrospectively at phase close-out, on 2026-07-31.
    It did not guide the work. See IntentSummary for the full record; in short:

    WHY: Phase 3 executed against docs/plans/active/RM-AGENT-RELIABILITY §3 and amendments
    A10-A16 rather than against a bundle plan.xml, so the bundle held spec.xml only. That
    blocked archival (change.applied-plan-missing) and left ngrace status reporting
    states=needs-plan for finished work.

    NOT A DETECTION FAILURE: ngrace status reported needs-plan correctly and continuously
    from the moment the spec was approved. The signal was right and was ignored, through
    four review rounds.

    PREVENTION, WITH AN OWNER: Phase 5's transition surface (D11, D14) gates on declared
    evidence. A gate refusing `applied` without a plan is exactly that shape, and turns
    this from an intention into a mechanism. Until Phase 5 ships, the discipline is manual:
    Phase 4 authors its bundle plan.xml before execution, not after. Recorded in A17.

    The task breakdown below is the real commit sequence, not an invention. It is honest
    about being written after the fact.
  -->
  <C-RUN-LEDGER>
    <IntentSummary>
      Land the run ledger, the regenerable cursor, and the fold protocol per D1, D2 and D3.

      RETROSPECTIVE EXCEPTION (A17): this plan was written at close-out on 2026-07-31 and did
      not guide execution. Phase 3 was driven by docs/plans/active/RM-AGENT-RELIABILITY §3
      together with amendments A10-A16, and its bundle carried spec.xml alone until now. The
      omission blocked archival — change.applied-plan-missing requires an applied plan beside
      an applied spec — while leaving the bundle reporting states=needs-plan in ngrace status
      for work that was finished. It is recorded as an exception rather than repaired silently,
      because a plan that implied it had guided the work would be a false record, and that is
      the failure this whole track exists to prevent. Future bundles carry a plan.xml authored
      before execution. Prevention is owned by Phase 5's transition surface, not by good
      intentions.
    </IntentSummary>
